# The Docker build context is the repository root — Railway's config-as-code
# does not follow Root Directory, so `apps/rembg/Dockerfile` builds from the
# root and would otherwise upload the whole workspace to the builder.
#
# **Railpack reads this file too**, which is the reason it is short. It is not
# only the Dockerfile build that is filtered by it: the `web`, `admin` and
# `worker` services print "Found .dockerignore file, applying filters" in their
# own build logs, so anything excluded here is excluded from three Node builds
# that were working before it existed. Only things no build can need belong
# below — generated output, caches and secrets. When in doubt, leave it in.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
.turbo
**/.turbo
**/.next
.git

# Never into an image, even one that does not read them.
.env
.env.local
**/.env
**/.env.local

# Python, from apps/rembg only.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
apps/rembg/.venv
